{"schema_version":1,"architecture_version":3,"workstream_id":"AAYS_21_SLOT_SAFE_PARALLEL_V1","slot_id":"height_difference_3","task_id":"height_difference_3-canonical-api-measurement-20260721-01","continuation_key":"6e8e709b6bad7b9807055e2b8b5de98cd4945ee3dee57825e72ba1b824eadd0f","created_at":"2026-08-01T10:32:00Z","claim_commit_sha":"e58836a072ead98132ef787f83d8c4d7e3bb2e90","state":"GEOMETRY_VALIDITY_REPAIR_PRECISION_OVERLAY_AND_MASK_STABILITY_GATE_QUALIFIED_RUNTIME_HELD","purpose":"Qualify Simple Features validity, make-valid provenance, fixed-precision overlay robustness, canonical geometry change metrics and raster-mask membership stability without executing blocked runtime or promoting numeric values.","official_controls":[{"id":"SIMPLE_FEATURE_VALIDITY_AND_PREDICATE_PREREQUISITES","sources":["https://gdal.org/en/stable/user/geometry_validity.html","https://gdal.org/en/stable/doxygen/classOGRGeometry.html","https://docs.ogc.org/is/21-045r1/21-045r1.html"],"facts":["Simple Features geometry validity must be established before spatial predicates and overlay operations are trusted.","GDAL documents that invalid geometries can produce incorrect intersection results and that validity checks do not cover all cross-feature gaps, overlaps, spikes or slivers.","Contains, covers, intersection and related predicates do not automatically validate their inputs."],"decision":"For every source and repaired parcel geometry persist is_valid, is_valid_reason, geometry type, emptiness, dimensionality, ring/part counts and the exact GEOS/GDAL/Shapely versions before any point-in-polygon, intersection or mask operation."},{"id":"MAKE_VALID_METHOD_AND_REPAIR_PROVENANCE","sources":["https://shapely.readthedocs.io/en/latest/reference/shapely.make_valid.html","https://gdal.org/en/stable/doxygen/classOGRGeometry.html"],"facts":["Shapely make_valid offers linework and structure strategies with materially different repair semantics.","Repair can return complex or lower-dimensional collections and can alter ring ordering or duplicated points.","A valid post-repair geometry does not by itself prove that the intended parcel surface was preserved."],"decision":"Record original and repaired WKB/WKT hashes, repair method, keep_collapsed, input/output types, polygon/lower-dimension part census, vertex/ring counts, validity reasons, and reject any lower-dimensional or non-polygon residue unless explicitly removed and documented."},{"id":"FIXED_PRECISION_GRID_AND_OVERLAY_ROBUSTNESS","sources":["https://shapely.readthedocs.io/en/latest/reference/shapely.set_precision.html","https://libgeos.org/doxygen/classgeos_1_1operation_1_1overlayng_1_1OverlayNG.html","https://libgeos.org/doxygen/classgeos_1_1geom_1_1PrecisionModel.html"],"facts":["Shapely uses double precision by default unless a grid size is set.","GEOS OverlayNG can use a fixed precision model with snap rounding to improve robustness and produce validly rounded output.","Floating precision overlay can raise topology errors or produce results sensitive to numerical rounding."],"decision":"Pin a BNG metre precision grid and mode, persist pre/post precision hashes and coordinate counts, and run overlay/mask sensitivity at the pinned grid plus a documented adjacent grid; reject topology errors, collapses or unstable acceptance."},{"id":"CANONICAL_NORMALIZATION_AND_CHANGE_QUANTIFICATION","sources":["https://shapely.readthedocs.io/en/2.1.1/reference/shapely.equals_exact.html","https://shapely.readthedocs.io/en/2.1.1/reference/shapely.normalize.html","https://gdal.org/en/stable/doxygen/classOGRGeometry.html"],"facts":["Topological equality can be true even when coordinate order or structure differs.","Normalization is useful for stable structural comparison and hashing.","Repair or precision reduction can change area, perimeter, parts, rings and boundary location while remaining valid."],"decision":"Normalize before deduplication and hashing; persist topological equality, normalized exact equality, area/perimeter delta, symmetric-difference area and ratio, Hausdorff/boundary displacement, part/ring/vertex deltas and explicit pass/fail thresholds."},{"id":"RASTER_MASK_MEMBERSHIP_STABILITY","sources":["https://rasterio.readthedocs.io/en/stable/api/rasterio.mask.html","https://rasterio.readthedocs.io/en/stable/api/rasterio.features.html"],"facts":["With all_touched false Rasterio generally includes pixels whose centers lie within the polygon.","Mask membership depends on the geometry coordinates, affine transform and selected pixel-centre rule.","Small boundary changes can alter valid-cell membership and therefore P05/P95 statistics for small parcels."],"decision":"Persist the exact mask bitmap hash, selected row/column census, valid and nodata counts, changed-cell count between original/repaired/precision variants, mask-area ratio and P05/P95 sensitivity; reject candidates whose acceptance or robust height difference is unstable."}],"repository_controls":[{"id":"AAYS_008_MAKE_VALID_PROVENANCE_GAP","path":"docs/chatgpt_status/topography/shards/height_difference_3/automation/008_match_hmlr_inspire_gml.py","sha":"5240a20ea0d65fa99af845d15e8219daf1287cf2","facts":["The script transforms source geometry, calls make_valid when is_valid is false, then accepts non-empty positive-area Polygon/MultiPolygon results.","It records only the accepted geometry type, rounded area, WKT/GeoJSON and point coverage.","It does not record the original invalidity reason, repair method, before/after hashes, lower-dimensional residues, part/ring/vertex deltas, precision model or area/symmetric-difference change."],"decision":"Preserve the pinned matcher and require a supplementary geometry-repair provenance manifest before the accepted WKT can be measured."},{"id":"AAYS_009_PRECISION_AND_MASK_STABILITY_GAP","path":"docs/chatgpt_status/topography/shards/height_difference_3/automation/009_sample_ea_dtm_and_os_terrain50.py","sha":"42ac87801263b6b94532c0897dbb5211b79ebeb1","facts":["The measurement script requires the matched WKT to be valid and uses intersects/covers plus Rasterio mask with all_touched false.","It does not bind a geometry precision grid, normalized canonical hash, overlay robustness result, mask bitmap hash or changed-cell sensitivity.","It therefore cannot yet prove that make_valid or coordinate rounding leaves the P95-P05 result and promotion decision stable."],"decision":"Require a per-candidate precision/overlay/mask-stability manifest and fail closed on topology errors, cell-membership changes beyond threshold or acceptance-state changes."}],"quality_checks":[{"index":1,"group":"SIMPLE_FEATURE_VALIDITY_AND_PREDICATE_PREREQUISITES","check":"official_simple_features_validity_bound","result":"PASS"},{"index":2,"group":"SIMPLE_FEATURE_VALIDITY_AND_PREDICATE_PREREQUISITES","check":"gdal_invalid_overlay_risk_bound","result":"PASS"},{"index":3,"group":"SIMPLE_FEATURE_VALIDITY_AND_PREDICATE_PREREQUISITES","check":"input_is_valid_required","result":"PASS"},{"index":4,"group":"SIMPLE_FEATURE_VALIDITY_AND_PREDICATE_PREREQUISITES","check":"input_is_valid_reason_required","result":"PASS"},{"index":5,"group":"SIMPLE_FEATURE_VALIDITY_AND_PREDICATE_PREREQUISITES","check":"geometry_type_and_dimension_required","result":"PASS"},{"index":6,"group":"SIMPLE_FEATURE_VALIDITY_AND_PREDICATE_PREREQUISITES","check":"empty_and_finite_area_rejected","result":"PASS"},{"index":7,"group":"SIMPLE_FEATURE_VALIDITY_AND_PREDICATE_PREREQUISITES","check":"predicate_inputs_validated","result":"PASS"},{"index":8,"group":"SIMPLE_FEATURE_VALIDITY_AND_PREDICATE_PREREQUISITES","check":"candidate_original_validity_readback","result":"HELD_RUNTIME"},{"index":9,"group":"MAKE_VALID_METHOD_AND_REPAIR_PROVENANCE","check":"official_make_valid_methods_bound","result":"PASS"},{"index":10,"group":"MAKE_VALID_METHOD_AND_REPAIR_PROVENANCE","check":"repair_method_required","result":"PASS"},{"index":11,"group":"MAKE_VALID_METHOD_AND_REPAIR_PROVENANCE","check":"keep_collapsed_required","result":